1
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:35,000
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:37,680
[Episode 27]

3
00:01:41,759 --> 00:01:42,509
Until new evidence

4
00:01:42,509 --> 00:01:43,120
appears,

5
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:44,120
it's impossible.

6
00:01:44,840 --> 00:01:46,500
What about the pager message?

7
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:47,900
That can be explained.

8
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:50,640
Gaoxin Road

9
00:01:51,310 --> 00:01:52,840
wasn't the primary crime scene.

10
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:53,789
He drove away

11
00:01:53,789 --> 00:01:55,400
at 11:57 that night

12
00:01:55,430 --> 00:01:56,479
from Gaoxin Road.

13
00:01:56,890 --> 00:01:57,890
He said he got home

14
00:01:57,920 --> 00:01:59,070
around 1 AM.

15
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:00,640
There is

16
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:01,840
a one‑hour window

17
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:04,230
during which his whereabouts are unknown.

18
00:02:04,230 --> 00:02:05,120
It took him

19
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:06,050
about 20 minutes

20
00:02:06,510 --> 00:02:08,370
to drive from Gaoxin Road to here.

21
00:02:08,590 --> 00:02:09,310
He could have easily

22
00:02:09,310 --> 00:02:10,310
committed the crime here,

23
00:02:10,310 --> 00:02:11,310
cleaned up the scene,

24
00:02:11,310 --> 00:02:12,240
and made it home.

25
00:02:12,750 --> 00:02:13,960
He'd even have had time to spare.

26
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:15,080
No one can verify

27
00:02:15,630 --> 00:02:16,490
when he got home

28
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:18,280
except his wife.

29
00:02:18,630 --> 00:02:19,800
And I've always felt

30
00:02:18,820 --> 00:02:20,360
[Got a passenger. I'll be home late.]

31
00:02:20,910 --> 00:02:22,170
that what his wife said

32
00:02:22,870 --> 00:02:24,329
is not entirely credible.

33
00:02:25,910 --> 00:02:27,720
Prosecutor Zhang and I looked

34
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:28,560
into the taxi company's

35
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:29,840
shift handover records from back then.

36
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:31,430
Yan Jicai did sign off

37
00:02:31,430 --> 00:02:32,590
and hand over his taxi

38
00:02:32,590 --> 00:02:33,720
at 12:40 that night.

39
00:02:34,420 --> 00:02:35,360
And from the taxi company's

40
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:35,930
parking lot

41
00:02:35,930 --> 00:02:36,920
to his home,

42
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:37,750
it really does take

43
00:02:37,750 --> 00:02:38,750
about 20 minutes.

44
00:02:39,310 --> 00:02:40,630
And that girl just willingly

45
00:02:40,630 --> 00:02:41,750
let him bring her here?

46
00:02:41,750 --> 00:02:43,280
Didn't she fight back?

47
00:02:43,470 --> 00:02:44,710
She could have been subdued

48
00:02:44,710 --> 00:02:46,360
or rendered unconscious.

49
00:02:46,590 --> 00:02:47,400
With what?

50
00:02:47,590 --> 00:02:48,120
Tied up?

51
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,630
Knocked out? Drugged?

52
00:02:49,630 --> 00:02:50,910
There should have been
some physical traces.

53
00:02:50,910 --> 00:02:53,170
Does the autopsy report show any of that?

54
00:02:55,150 --> 00:02:56,750
She was tricked into coming.

55
00:02:58,310 --> 00:02:59,240
A smooth talker,

56
00:03:00,980 --> 00:03:01,780
just like you.

57
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:08,560
That girl was worn down by his words?

58
00:03:09,430 --> 00:03:10,360
Captain Donkey.

59
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:13,080
Stubborn as a mule.

60
00:03:21,630 --> 00:03:22,360
Captain Lyu.

61
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:23,870
This place is too remote.
It's hard to get a cab.

62
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:25,070
Let me give you a ride.

63
00:03:30,150 --> 00:03:30,880
Captain Lyu.

64
00:03:34,630 --> 00:03:36,430
Are you really going to walk back?

65
00:03:36,430 --> 00:03:37,630
Let me give you a ride.

66
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:41,630
You're using the procuratorate's car

67
00:03:41,630 --> 00:03:43,430
for personal errands so openly?

68
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:45,030
If I say I have permission
for personal visits,

69
00:03:45,030 --> 00:03:46,230
would you believe it?

70
00:03:47,590 --> 00:03:49,320
You're siding with outsiders.

71
00:03:49,430 --> 00:03:51,160
Does your leader support that?

72
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:52,240
Our leader said

73
00:03:52,710 --> 00:03:54,510
that the law is made by the state,

74
00:03:54,579 --> 00:03:55,680
and that the procuratorate is the state's

75
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:56,610
judicial organ,

76
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:58,910
and so is the public security bureau.

77
00:03:58,910 --> 00:04:01,030
He said it's good
to have a sense of honor,

78
00:04:01,030 --> 00:04:04,160
but we can't cover up for each other
just because of that.

79
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:06,220
I added that last line myself.

80
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:06,870
Let's go. Let's go.

81
00:04:06,870 --> 00:04:07,580
Alright, alright. No need.

82
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:08,510
Get in. Get in.

83
00:04:08,710 --> 00:04:09,800
Just listen to me!

84
00:04:09,910 --> 00:04:10,630
Hurry up!

85
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:21,040
Is it appropriate for me to talk

86
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:21,839
to Wang Danni?

87
00:04:22,830 --> 00:04:23,890
It's appropriate.

88
00:04:26,510 --> 00:04:28,240
I must have owed you something.

89
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:32,150
Last time I went there,

90
00:04:32,150 --> 00:04:33,040
her mother splashed tomato sauce

91
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:33,830
all over me.

92
00:04:37,150 --> 00:04:38,360
Maybe we should send

93
00:04:38,390 --> 00:04:39,260
a female colleague instead.

94
00:04:39,260 --> 00:04:40,940
She might be less resistant.

95
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,720
What about your girlfriend?

96
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:47,110
That's my wife.

97
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:49,070
Good for you.

98
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:52,600
She's like ten thousand miles away.

99
00:04:56,860 --> 00:04:57,930
I have to get

100
00:04:58,720 --> 00:04:59,920
to the bottom of this.

101
00:05:01,270 --> 00:05:02,120
I can't let my daughter

102
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:03,320
be wronged like this.

103
00:05:07,270 --> 00:05:08,560
Why are you staring at me?

104
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:09,450
Yan Jicai's wife

105
00:05:09,450 --> 00:05:10,780
must think the same way,

106
00:05:11,070 --> 00:05:13,330
but she doesn't have your capabilities.

107
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:19,600
Forget it if you don't want to help.

108
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:21,330
Pretend that I never asked you.

109
00:05:32,870 --> 00:05:33,310
Miss.

110
00:05:33,730 --> 00:05:34,510
What happened to you?

111
00:05:34,510 --> 00:05:35,040
I'm fine.

112
00:05:35,130 --> 00:05:35,720
What happened?

113
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:36,330
Are you hurt?

114
00:05:36,330 --> 00:05:37,930
I'm fine. It's tomato paste.

115
00:05:40,870 --> 00:05:42,720
You're Zhou Pu's daughter, right?

116
00:05:42,720 --> 00:05:44,120
You're that prosecutor!

117
00:05:45,310 --> 00:05:45,800
Miss.

118
00:05:46,190 --> 00:05:48,190
Are you also going to Wang Danni's place?

119
00:05:48,190 --> 00:05:48,600
Yes.

120
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:50,950
You're that...

121
00:05:51,630 --> 00:05:52,360
Captain Lyu!

122
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:54,070
Miss.

123
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:55,360
What do you do?

124
00:05:56,050 --> 00:05:57,050
I'm a journalist.

125
00:05:57,070 --> 00:05:57,750
Are you also here to see

126
00:05:57,750 --> 00:05:58,950
Wang Danni's mother?

127
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:01,190
Then there's no need to go.

128
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:01,720
Why?

129
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:04,970
She's making tomato paste now.

130
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:09,310
Does Wang Danni's family

131
00:06:09,310 --> 00:06:10,840
run a tomato paste factory?

132
00:06:11,630 --> 00:06:12,800
You journalists

133
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,600
just want to stir up trouble.

134
00:06:20,070 --> 00:06:21,750
What do you know about the situation?

135
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:22,630
Do you know Wang Danni

136
00:06:22,630 --> 00:06:23,480
and Lyu Siyi?

137
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:28,360
How long have you known Captain Lyu?

138
00:06:29,270 --> 00:06:30,400
Can I interview you?

139
00:06:30,870 --> 00:06:32,470
I'm just a dutiful driver.

140
00:06:33,030 --> 00:06:33,750
Aren't you and your girlfriend

141
00:06:33,750 --> 00:06:34,810
both prosecutors?

142
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:36,630
How do you know

143
00:06:36,630 --> 00:06:37,830
she's my girlfriend?

144
00:06:38,830 --> 00:06:39,680
A journalist

145
00:06:41,310 --> 00:06:43,370
needs to have a sharp nose for things.

146
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:46,120
I'm warning you. Don't write any nonsense.

147
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:47,650
If you dare write nonsense,

148
00:06:47,830 --> 00:06:48,390
I'll definitely come

149
00:06:48,390 --> 00:06:49,650
after your newspaper.

150
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:51,190
Don't worry.

151
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:53,220
I'm a journalist with ideals.

152
00:06:53,330 --> 00:06:54,360
What I want is the truth.

153
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,390
I will never believe

154
00:06:55,390 --> 00:06:57,120
Wang Danni's one-sided story.

155
00:07:04,390 --> 00:07:05,680
I guess Wang Danni

156
00:07:07,190 --> 00:07:08,160
doesn't even dare to accept

157
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:09,090
your interview.

158
00:07:10,630 --> 00:07:12,390
How do you know that?

159
00:07:24,310 --> 00:07:25,370
Put it down gently.

160
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:26,410
Handle with care.

161
00:07:26,410 --> 00:07:26,920
Okay.

162
00:07:26,950 --> 00:07:28,120
Yes, handle with care.

163
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:29,120
Stack them tight.

164
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:32,000
Yes, stuff them all in
and stack them tight.

165
00:07:32,950 --> 00:07:33,760
Ride slowly!

166
00:07:34,310 --> 00:07:36,170
Can you afford to pay if it breaks?

167
00:07:36,310 --> 00:07:37,909
Boss, we're ready to depart.

168
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:41,460
Keep a close eye

169
00:07:41,630 --> 00:07:43,040
on this truck of goods on the road.

170
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:43,630
Got it?

171
00:07:43,830 --> 00:07:44,190
Okay.

172
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:45,270
-Go.
-Okay.

173
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:46,530
You can't leave!

174
00:07:46,950 --> 00:07:48,360
You can't transport these goods.

175
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:49,600
These are frozen assets.

176
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:51,360
You need approval from the court.

177
00:07:51,360 --> 00:07:52,420
Where are you from?

178
00:07:52,870 --> 00:07:54,070
I am the plaintiff's lawyer

179
00:07:54,070 --> 00:07:54,950
for this case.

180
00:07:57,360 --> 00:07:57,800
Go.

181
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:58,430
Drive.

182
00:07:59,070 --> 00:08:00,000
You can't leave!

183
00:08:00,430 --> 00:08:01,630
I've been watching you for days.

184
00:08:01,630 --> 00:08:03,230
I knew you'd pull this trick!

185
00:08:03,810 --> 00:08:05,410
I'm not wasting words on you.

186
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:07,240
Go to the court if you have a problem!

187
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:09,720
I'm here on behalf
of the Enforcement Division.

188
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:10,980
On behalf of the court!

189
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:13,120
You're on behalf of the court?

190
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:14,780
You think I don't know the law?

191
00:08:15,430 --> 00:08:15,930
Drive!

192
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:16,680
Freeze!

193
00:08:17,430 --> 00:08:18,960
Let's see who dares to move!

194
00:08:21,430 --> 00:08:22,230
Take him away!

195
00:08:22,390 --> 00:08:23,270
Murder! Murder!

196
00:08:23,270 --> 00:08:24,740
-Take him away!
-There's a murder here!

197
00:08:24,740 --> 00:08:26,210
Help! Help!

198
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:26,750
Hurry!

199
00:08:26,750 --> 00:08:28,330
Call the police! Call the police!

200
00:08:28,330 --> 00:08:29,190
I'm out! I'm out!

201
00:08:29,190 --> 00:08:29,850
Let go of me.

202
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:31,680
Murder!

203
00:08:31,870 --> 00:08:33,039
Murder! Murder!

204
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:34,600
-Help!
-Come out!

205
00:08:34,750 --> 00:08:36,120
Help! Call the police!

206
00:08:36,150 --> 00:08:37,200
Someone's dying!

207
00:08:37,390 --> 00:08:38,919
They're gonna break my leg!

208
00:08:39,950 --> 00:08:41,780
I didn't move! I really didn't!

209
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:42,909
Help!

210
00:08:42,909 --> 00:08:43,710
Stop yelling!

211
00:08:48,790 --> 00:08:49,360
You win.

212
00:08:49,910 --> 00:08:50,370
You win.

213
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:54,440
I'll come to you
if I have a lawsuit in the future.

214
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:55,440
What's your name?

215
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:57,390
Qin Zhigao.

216
00:08:58,630 --> 00:08:59,670
Nice to meet you.

217
00:09:04,310 --> 00:09:05,670
Once we receive the invoice,

218
00:09:05,670 --> 00:09:06,950
I'll transfer the money right away.

219
00:09:06,950 --> 00:09:07,320
Okay, okay.

220
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:07,850
200,000.

221
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:08,750
Okay, okay.

222
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:09,900
Mr. Qin,

223
00:09:10,030 --> 00:09:11,150
you really have a way with things.

224
00:09:11,150 --> 00:09:13,000
I really thought those two million

225
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,790
were gone for good.

226
00:09:14,900 --> 00:09:16,230
It wasn't much trouble.

227
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:17,710
In Nanyu,

228
00:09:17,870 --> 00:09:20,130
my influence still carries some weight.

229
00:09:20,390 --> 00:09:21,180
Yes, yes.

230
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:22,640
I'm impressed.

231
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:24,520
Zhao, bring some tea!

232
00:09:25,750 --> 00:09:26,330
This is

233
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:27,880
my personal gesture of compensation.

234
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:28,970
Didn't you lose

235
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:29,840
a camera?

236
00:09:30,030 --> 00:09:31,030
This is brand new.

237
00:09:33,730 --> 00:09:35,090
How could I accept this?

238
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:36,320
Why not?

239
00:09:36,670 --> 00:09:37,670
Our company will have

240
00:09:37,670 --> 00:09:38,870
plenty of business in the future.

241
00:09:38,870 --> 00:09:40,440
Let's cooperate more in the future.

242
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:41,370
With you around,

243
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:42,720
I feel at ease.

244
00:09:42,750 --> 00:09:43,680
Come on, take it.

245
00:09:44,240 --> 00:09:46,200
Okay, this is great.

246
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:47,850
I'm at your service!

247
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:48,480
Good.

248
00:09:49,010 --> 00:09:50,120
I won't keep you any longer.

249
00:09:50,120 --> 00:09:51,050
I'm leaving now.

250
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:52,630
I'll treat you to a meal next time.

251
00:09:52,630 --> 00:09:53,390
Okay, I'll walk you out.

252
00:09:53,390 --> 00:09:54,320
No need. No need.

253
00:09:54,790 --> 00:09:55,390
Goodbye.

254
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:56,780
Ms. Gui.

255
00:09:59,440 --> 00:10:01,480
Can we take a photo together

256
00:10:01,550 --> 00:10:02,550
with this camera?

257
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:04,360
Sure.

258
00:10:05,110 --> 00:10:06,710
One, two, three.

259
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:11,850
[Jianzheng Law Firm]

260
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:16,840
Come in.

261
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:25,420
This place is really nice.

262
00:10:25,670 --> 00:10:26,510
In just a couple of days,

263
00:10:26,510 --> 00:10:27,570
how did you find it?

264
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:28,600
It's Mei's place.

265
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:30,620
Just put your stuff there.

266
00:10:31,590 --> 00:10:33,330
She's traveling around China.

267
00:10:33,550 --> 00:10:34,600
She won't be back for a year or two,

268
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:36,730
so she asked me to look after the place.

269
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:38,150
This room is mine.

270
00:10:38,150 --> 00:10:39,150
That one is yours.

271
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:43,790
Is this appropriate?

272
00:10:43,790 --> 00:10:45,590
What's inappropriate about it?

273
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:47,140
Don't let your imagination run wild.

274
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:48,740
Otherwise, I'll chop you up.

275
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:49,510
Well,

276
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:50,750
I mean...

277
00:10:51,710 --> 00:10:53,350
I'm defending Hu Xudong,

278
00:10:54,130 --> 00:10:55,560
and you're a judge.

279
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,000
Is it appropriate for us to live together?

280
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:58,840
Don't worry.

281
00:10:59,730 --> 00:11:00,670
Our Deputy Court Pres. Yu

282
00:11:00,670 --> 00:11:01,330
won't let me

283
00:11:01,340 --> 00:11:02,740
be assigned to this case.

284
00:11:03,030 --> 00:11:04,760
Don't you know him well enough?

285
00:11:07,030 --> 00:11:08,160
Strictly speaking,

286
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:10,080
you don't have to recuse yourself

287
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:12,030
unless one of the parties requests it.

288
00:11:12,030 --> 00:11:13,090
Alright, alright.

289
00:11:13,490 --> 00:11:14,490
Mr. Jurist.

290
00:11:14,820 --> 00:11:15,550
I know.

291
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:17,560
It's not about recusal.

292
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:19,330
It's that my disciplinary period
hasn't ended yet.

293
00:11:19,330 --> 00:11:20,120
I can't even serve

294
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:21,380
as an associate judge.

295
00:11:21,550 --> 00:11:23,440
And even if I were allowed to hear it,

296
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:25,170
I would voluntarily withdraw.

297
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:26,840
The public opinion on this case

298
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:28,170
is too heated right now.

299
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:30,940
I can't put pressure on the court.

300
00:11:37,660 --> 00:11:38,690
When are you going

301
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:40,380
to get Hu Xudong's signature?

302
00:11:42,510 --> 00:11:44,240
I'll go see my mentor first.

303
00:11:45,390 --> 00:11:47,190
Then I'll go to Hu Xudong's place

304
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:48,450
to talk

305
00:11:48,470 --> 00:11:49,630
to his father and brother,

306
00:11:49,630 --> 00:11:52,140
trying to obtain the power of attorney
for the defense.

307
00:11:52,140 --> 00:11:52,810
His family

308
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:53,910
doesn't live in the village anymore.

309
00:11:53,910 --> 00:11:54,970
They moved to town.

310
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:55,840
Why?

311
00:11:56,670 --> 00:11:58,600
They've become public enemies
in the village.

312
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:00,330
They can't stay there anymore.

313
00:12:05,030 --> 00:12:06,320
The case file really got sent back?

314
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:06,750
Yes.

315
00:12:07,240 --> 00:12:08,500
The facts are unclear,

316
00:12:08,510 --> 00:12:09,880
and the evidence is insufficient.

317
00:12:09,880 --> 00:12:11,150
Even if you forced through a prosecution,

318
00:12:11,150 --> 00:12:11,960
eventually the court would

319
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:13,020
send the file back.

320
00:12:13,150 --> 00:12:14,870
I've already asked
the public security bureau

321
00:12:14,870 --> 00:12:17,270
to conduct supplementary investigation.

322
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:18,000
Great.

323
00:12:19,630 --> 00:12:20,390
Have a seat.

324
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:20,960
Okay.

325
00:12:22,230 --> 00:12:23,870
I've heard the public pressure

326
00:12:23,870 --> 00:12:25,230
is pretty intense right now.

327
00:12:25,230 --> 00:12:26,300
Authorities at every level

328
00:12:26,300 --> 00:12:27,870
are pushing for a speedy resolution.

329
00:12:27,870 --> 00:12:29,820
And Yin Ping's uncle

330
00:12:30,030 --> 00:12:30,960
has organized the whole village

331
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:32,470
to sign and press their fingerprints
on a petition.

332
00:12:32,470 --> 00:12:33,440
It's not just the police.

333
00:12:33,440 --> 00:12:34,480
Our procuratorate

334
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:35,410
and I personally

335
00:12:35,670 --> 00:12:37,200
are under a lot of pressure.

336
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:38,820
But we just have to bear it.

337
00:12:39,200 --> 00:12:39,720
Mentor.

338
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:40,800
That's right.

339
00:12:41,150 --> 00:12:42,510
Our procuratorate can't keep

340
00:12:42,510 --> 00:12:44,310
letting public opinion sway us.

341
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:45,670
Don't...

342
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:47,290
call me Mentor anymore.

343
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,600
Once you become his defense lawyer,

344
00:12:49,870 --> 00:12:51,630
we will be opponents in court.

345
00:12:53,030 --> 00:12:54,550
It's not like that, Mentor.

346
00:12:54,550 --> 00:12:55,790
I think our goals

347
00:12:55,790 --> 00:12:56,520
are the same.

348
00:12:56,750 --> 00:12:57,600
We both seek

349
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:58,480
legal justice.

350
00:12:58,640 --> 00:12:59,670
We've already assigned

351
00:12:59,670 --> 00:13:01,400
a legal aid lawyer to Hu Xudong.

352
00:13:01,870 --> 00:13:04,080
But his family wants
to find one themselves.

353
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:05,390
You are the perfect candidate.

354
00:13:05,390 --> 00:13:05,960
Alright.

355
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:07,790
Then I'll go see his family

356
00:13:07,790 --> 00:13:08,720
this afternoon.

357
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:10,910
And then I'll go see Hu Xudong.

358
00:13:12,870 --> 00:13:14,630
I... I remember you said this before.

359
00:13:14,630 --> 00:13:16,870
It's hard for lawyers
to meet clients, review files,

360
00:13:16,870 --> 00:13:18,130
and collect evidence.

361
00:13:18,510 --> 00:13:19,110
It is hard.

362
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:20,080
It really is.

363
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:22,550
And this is also a common phenomenon

364
00:13:22,550 --> 00:13:23,320
nowadays.

365
00:13:24,550 --> 00:13:25,840
But for this case,

366
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:27,840
I'll do what I can within my authority

367
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:29,080
to create the conditions

368
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:30,340
for you to work freely.

369
00:13:32,150 --> 00:13:32,910
Mentor.

370
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:35,690
What's this?

371
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:36,720
Thanks for your support.

372
00:13:36,720 --> 00:13:38,120
Thanks for your support.

373
00:13:39,190 --> 00:13:39,940
If I tied

374
00:13:40,170 --> 00:13:41,200
one of my opponent's hands behind his back

375
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:41,740
when playing basketball,

376
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:43,270
what would be the point of my victory?

377
00:13:43,270 --> 00:13:44,750
Yeah, what would be the point?

378
00:13:44,750 --> 00:13:45,610
No point at all.

379
00:13:45,900 --> 00:13:49,800
[No. 2 Detention Center
of Binjiang City, Dongjiang Province]

380
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:25,240
Hello, Hu Xudong.

381
00:14:25,550 --> 00:14:26,550
I'm Chen Yizhong,

382
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:27,320
a lawyer.

383
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,730
I came all the way from Beijing.

384
00:14:30,490 --> 00:14:32,030
I've been entrusted by your family

385
00:14:32,030 --> 00:14:32,960
to be your

386
00:14:33,320 --> 00:14:34,270
defense lawyer.

387
00:14:34,760 --> 00:14:35,910
I have a power of attorney here.

388
00:14:35,910 --> 00:14:36,980
I'll need you to sign it.

389
00:14:36,980 --> 00:14:37,530
No need.

390
00:14:40,570 --> 00:14:41,480
They already sent

391
00:14:41,480 --> 00:14:42,880
someone like you before.

392
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:45,220
It was useless.

393
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:50,550
The one you're talking about

394
00:14:50,550 --> 00:14:52,750
is a court-appointed legal aid lawyer.

395
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:54,710
They are quite different from us.

396
00:14:55,050 --> 00:14:56,320
By the way, your brother

397
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:57,670
specifically asked me to tell you

398
00:14:57,670 --> 00:14:59,000
that he still hopes

399
00:14:59,030 --> 00:15:00,630
I can be your defense lawyer.

400
00:15:02,910 --> 00:15:03,550
How much?

401
00:15:06,510 --> 00:15:06,960
Did they give you

402
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:08,960
all the money I saved for my wedding?

403
00:15:09,910 --> 00:15:12,640
Is money more important
than your life right now?

404
00:15:13,660 --> 00:15:15,790
Even ten lawyers won't make a difference.

405
00:15:15,790 --> 00:15:17,050
Don't waste your time.

406
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:18,810
What do you mean by that?

407
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:20,290
What do you think I mean?

408
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:22,050
What else could it mean?

409
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,930
They're deliberately framing me.

410
00:15:25,150 --> 00:15:26,210
Can't you see that?

411
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:28,460
The police, the procuratorate,

412
00:15:28,910 --> 00:15:29,770
the villagers,

413
00:15:30,750 --> 00:15:32,010
and those journalists

414
00:15:33,360 --> 00:15:34,240
all believe

415
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:35,500
that I'm the murderer.

416
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:38,900
What else can I say?

417
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:41,480
What can you possibly do?

418
00:15:43,670 --> 00:15:44,750
Just let them sentence me
however they want.

419
00:15:44,750 --> 00:15:45,280
Alright?

420
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:47,300
I want to go out.

421
00:15:48,170 --> 00:15:49,440
Open the door! I want to go out!

422
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:50,360
I'm here

423
00:15:50,360 --> 00:15:51,120
to defend you.

424
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:52,200
I want to go out!

425
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:53,670
Hu Xudong,

426
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:55,600
if you keep this attitude,

427
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:56,340
then no one can save you.

428
00:15:56,340 --> 00:15:57,600
I don't need you to save me.

429
00:15:57,600 --> 00:15:58,600
No one can save me!

430
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:01,020
Do you understand?

431
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:15,920
Off you go.

432
00:16:19,150 --> 00:16:20,000
Mentor.

433
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:24,840
What's wrong now?

434
00:16:29,870 --> 00:16:31,000
Mentor, do you want

435
00:16:31,510 --> 00:16:32,960
to see Yan Jicai again?

436
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:34,720
No need.

437
00:16:36,670 --> 00:16:38,750
He'll get worked up again, and maybe he'll

438
00:16:38,750 --> 00:16:40,080
even hit the wall again.

439
00:16:40,120 --> 00:16:42,030
I'll find a chance to talk to him.

440
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:44,060
I'm still here.

441
00:16:44,750 --> 00:16:46,170
He can feel more at ease.

442
00:16:47,740 --> 00:16:49,270
Aren't you about to retire?

443
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:52,870
I've already submitted a report

444
00:16:52,870 --> 00:16:54,730
to postpone it for a while longer.

445
00:16:57,150 --> 00:16:58,420
Just for Yan Jicai?

446
00:16:59,750 --> 00:17:00,790
Not entirely.

447
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:03,440
I've got to get that

448
00:17:03,440 --> 00:17:04,900
second-class merit medal

449
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:07,530
back from Prosecutor You sooner or later.

450
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:12,550
It feels like I've been sentenced

451
00:17:12,550 --> 00:17:13,810
to life imprisonment.

452
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:17,270
Lihui,

453
00:17:17,770 --> 00:17:19,700
your fixed-term sentence is over.

454
00:17:23,480 --> 00:17:24,680
Mentor, don't worry.

455
00:17:24,980 --> 00:17:25,770
In Nanlu,

456
00:17:26,200 --> 00:17:28,860
I will definitely
continue the investigation.

457
00:17:30,380 --> 00:17:31,510
Before you leave,

458
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:33,520
I have some good news for you.

459
00:17:34,030 --> 00:17:35,090
Our procuratorate

460
00:17:35,440 --> 00:17:37,970
also attaches great importance
to this case.

461
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:40,270
We've formally sent an official letter

462
00:17:40,270 --> 00:17:42,030
asking the Nanlu Municipal Procuratorate

463
00:17:42,030 --> 00:17:43,960
to assist with the investigation.

464
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:45,310
Really?

465
00:17:50,310 --> 00:17:52,110
There is still a long road ahead.

466
00:17:53,110 --> 00:17:54,590
As long as we keep going,

467
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:58,440
we'll eventually see the light. Right?

468
00:18:03,070 --> 00:18:03,750
Off you go.

469
00:18:13,580 --> 00:18:18,030
[Procuratorate Office‌ in Bieshan Prison;
Xijiang Province Bieshan Prison]

470
00:18:38,710 --> 00:18:39,720
What else do you want to eat?

471
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:40,410
Tell me,

472
00:18:40,640 --> 00:18:42,500
and I'll bring it to you tomorrow.

473
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:45,480
Haven't my teammates come to see me?

474
00:18:52,510 --> 00:18:53,200
They're

475
00:18:54,120 --> 00:18:55,920
afraid of disturbing your rest.

476
00:18:57,750 --> 00:18:58,830
Not even one?

477
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:03,030
No.

478
00:19:03,270 --> 00:19:04,710
I told them that your mom was here,

479
00:19:04,710 --> 00:19:07,240
so it might not be convenient
for them to come.

480
00:19:10,890 --> 00:19:12,850
Not even Zhong Xiaohui?

481
00:19:13,550 --> 00:19:15,030
She's my best friend.

482
00:19:19,310 --> 00:19:20,510
Well, how about this?

483
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:21,850
When you get better,

484
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:23,440
I will invite them all

485
00:19:23,440 --> 00:19:24,240
to our place.

486
00:19:24,550 --> 00:19:25,950
We'll have a meal at home,

487
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:26,750
okay?

488
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:31,110
They won't come.

489
00:19:32,510 --> 00:19:33,710
I can't clear my name.

490
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:37,110
In their eyes,

491
00:19:39,110 --> 00:19:42,710
I'm a guilty person who attempted suicide
to escape punishment.

492
00:19:42,790 --> 00:19:44,120
Stop talking nonsense.

493
00:19:45,400 --> 00:19:46,660
There's no such thing.

494
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:47,610
Don't worry.

495
00:19:47,970 --> 00:19:48,590
About this matter,

496
00:19:48,590 --> 00:19:51,050
I will definitely find out the truth
for you.

497
00:19:52,160 --> 00:19:52,720
Look,

498
00:19:53,270 --> 00:19:54,270
the drip is finished.

499
00:19:54,270 --> 00:19:55,530
I'll go call the nurse.

500
00:19:56,590 --> 00:19:57,410
Nurse!

501
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:58,720
Nurse!

502
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:08,720
Mrs. Wang,

503
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:10,450
could you please open the door?

504
00:20:10,640 --> 00:20:12,640
I just want to talk to your daughter.

505
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:14,200
Open the door.

506
00:20:16,870 --> 00:20:18,200
If you come again, I'll call the police.

507
00:20:18,200 --> 00:20:19,130
Call the police?

508
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:20,340
I am the police.

509
00:20:23,310 --> 00:20:24,310
Don't splash anything at me again.

510
00:20:24,310 --> 00:20:25,000
If you do,

511
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:25,830
I won't go easy on you.

512
00:20:25,830 --> 00:20:26,880
Get lost!

513
00:20:29,110 --> 00:20:29,930
Let go!

514
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:30,830
I mean no harm.

515
00:20:30,850 --> 00:20:32,590
I just want to talk to your daughter.

516
00:20:32,590 --> 00:20:33,790
What is there to talk about?

517
00:20:33,790 --> 00:20:34,750
Get out!

518
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:35,880
-Get out!
-Wang Danni.

519
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:36,550
Get out!

520
00:20:36,720 --> 00:20:37,680
Wang Danni!

521
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:38,590
Get out!

522
00:20:38,590 --> 00:20:39,400
Do you know

523
00:20:40,030 --> 00:20:40,830
that my daughter

524
00:20:40,830 --> 00:20:42,240
can barely even stand up now?

525
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:43,640
Get out! Get out! Get out!

526
00:20:44,030 --> 00:20:44,680
Get out!

527
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:46,550
You can't just falsely accuse her
like this!

528
00:20:46,550 --> 00:20:47,030
Get out!

529
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:47,680
Mom.

530
00:20:47,750 --> 00:20:49,070
You're a cop, aren't you?

531
00:20:49,070 --> 00:20:49,800
So powerful!

532
00:20:49,830 --> 00:20:51,720
-Mom.
-Arrest me! Arrest me!

533
00:20:51,790 --> 00:20:52,750
Arrest me!

534
00:20:52,750 --> 00:20:53,200
Mom!

535
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:54,920
Get out!

536
00:20:54,940 --> 00:20:55,530
Mom!

537
00:20:58,310 --> 00:20:59,270
Let him in.

538
00:21:46,790 --> 00:21:48,030
What did the doctor say?

539
00:21:48,030 --> 00:21:48,630
He said...

540
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:51,730
that she might never be able...

541
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,930
to do gymnastics again in her life.

542
00:21:55,640 --> 00:21:56,310
Look.

543
00:21:56,670 --> 00:21:58,710
I work two jobs by myself.

544
00:21:59,640 --> 00:22:00,770
I've worked hard

545
00:22:00,810 --> 00:22:02,940
raising my daughter for over a decade.

546
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:04,350
I've endured so much hardship

547
00:22:04,350 --> 00:22:05,680
and suffered so much.

548
00:22:06,410 --> 00:22:08,650
And now it's all been destroyed

549
00:22:08,680 --> 00:22:09,790
by your daughter.

550
00:22:19,270 --> 00:22:20,070
You can leave.

551
00:22:20,920 --> 00:22:22,270
I can't leave. I...

552
00:22:22,290 --> 00:22:23,220
Leave!

553
00:22:47,590 --> 00:22:49,990
Do you think
you really know your daughter?

554
00:22:52,440 --> 00:22:53,240
Of course.

555
00:22:54,480 --> 00:22:55,070
I believe

556
00:22:55,070 --> 00:22:56,670
she wouldn't do such a thing.

557
00:22:57,440 --> 00:22:58,880
But Lyu Siyi told me

558
00:22:59,720 --> 00:23:01,780
that you never truly cared about her.

559
00:23:02,110 --> 00:23:03,040
Just like my mom,

560
00:23:03,440 --> 00:23:04,840
you're self-righteous.

561
00:23:05,380 --> 00:23:06,400
You think making some good food,

562
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:07,330
suffering a bit,

563
00:23:07,530 --> 00:23:08,070
and complaining

564
00:23:08,070 --> 00:23:09,530
about how hard your life is

565
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:11,330
makes you good parents,

566
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:12,720
as if we owe you.

567
00:23:17,880 --> 00:23:18,640
Our Siyi

568
00:23:18,640 --> 00:23:19,920
never snitched.

569
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:22,590
Your Coach Sun

570
00:23:22,590 --> 00:23:23,790
told me that himself.

571
00:23:25,110 --> 00:23:25,680
I know.

572
00:23:26,190 --> 00:23:27,790
Then at least on this matter,

573
00:23:28,510 --> 00:23:29,550
you wronged her.

574
00:23:34,350 --> 00:23:35,070
I admit

575
00:23:36,030 --> 00:23:37,110
I wronged her.

576
00:23:45,510 --> 00:23:46,160
Danni.

577
00:23:47,550 --> 00:23:48,720
You and our Siyi

578
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:51,130
are both still kids.

579
00:23:51,720 --> 00:23:52,960
I'm not a kid!

580
00:23:53,820 --> 00:23:55,070
Do you know how complicated

581
00:23:55,070 --> 00:23:56,600
the relationships between teammates
can be?

582
00:23:56,600 --> 00:23:57,440
Do you know how many people

583
00:23:57,440 --> 00:23:58,840
are hoping to replace me?

584
00:24:01,550 --> 00:24:03,280
I just want you to tell everyone

585
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:04,720
the truth.

586
00:24:09,920 --> 00:24:12,720
I've been a criminal police officer
my whole life.

587
00:24:13,440 --> 00:24:14,770
I've seen many bad guys.

588
00:24:19,750 --> 00:24:20,400
Kid,

589
00:24:21,440 --> 00:24:22,700
you're not one of them.

590
00:24:24,050 --> 00:24:24,850
You know what?

591
00:24:25,160 --> 00:24:27,090
Good people may make mistakes too.

592
00:24:27,880 --> 00:24:28,550
If someone

593
00:24:28,550 --> 00:24:30,160
carries such a big lie

594
00:24:30,380 --> 00:24:31,330
for a lifetime,

595
00:24:32,790 --> 00:24:34,480
their heart will be full of pain

596
00:24:34,480 --> 00:24:35,480
and torment.

597
00:24:38,480 --> 00:24:40,240
If I admit that I lied,

598
00:24:41,750 --> 00:24:42,680
what will you do?

599
00:24:50,160 --> 00:24:51,350
I will forgive you.

600
00:24:53,550 --> 00:24:54,240
But

601
00:24:56,270 --> 00:24:57,030
it's hard to say

602
00:24:57,030 --> 00:24:58,200
whether our Siyi

603
00:24:59,270 --> 00:25:00,600
will forgive you or not.

604
00:25:00,790 --> 00:25:02,250
I'm telling you the truth.

605
00:25:04,960 --> 00:25:07,020
What if it was your daughter who lied?

606
00:25:08,250 --> 00:25:09,450
What will you do then?

607
00:25:30,350 --> 00:25:31,150
What's wrong?

608
00:25:31,440 --> 00:25:32,170
Are you okay?

609
00:25:33,750 --> 00:25:34,950
What did he say to you?

610
00:25:36,240 --> 00:25:37,840
I need to tell you something.

611
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:39,510
I've wanted to say it for a long time.

612
00:25:39,510 --> 00:25:39,960
Okay.

613
00:25:40,350 --> 00:25:40,880
Go ahead.

614
00:25:41,780 --> 00:25:42,750
When I was 7,

615
00:25:43,550 --> 00:25:45,550
the first day you sent me to the team,

616
00:25:46,160 --> 00:25:47,400
I already hated gymnastics.

617
00:25:47,400 --> 00:25:48,400
I hated it so much!

618
00:25:54,270 --> 00:25:55,110
Is that it?

619
00:25:56,920 --> 00:25:57,520
That's it.

620
00:26:01,510 --> 00:26:03,110
I'll make you tomato shrimp.

621
00:26:04,880 --> 00:26:06,540
I just made some tomato paste.

622
00:26:20,750 --> 00:26:21,950
You've talked to her?

623
00:26:29,200 --> 00:26:29,920
Mr. Lyu,

624
00:26:30,250 --> 00:26:31,200
this topic I'm working on

625
00:26:31,200 --> 00:26:32,030
has huge significance.

626
00:26:32,030 --> 00:26:32,720
The tragedy

627
00:26:32,720 --> 00:26:34,410
caused by the current training
and selection mechanism.

628
00:26:34,410 --> 00:26:35,240
If this report gets published,

629
00:26:35,240 --> 00:26:36,130
not only will your daughter's injustice

630
00:26:36,130 --> 00:26:36,830
be cleared up,

631
00:26:36,830 --> 00:26:38,200
but it will also make the public reflect

632
00:26:38,200 --> 00:26:39,200
on the current...

633
00:26:41,040 --> 00:26:42,110
How do you know my daughter

634
00:26:42,110 --> 00:26:42,880
was wronged?

635
00:26:44,270 --> 00:26:45,030
Wasn't she?

636
00:26:46,750 --> 00:26:48,210
Have you investigated it?

637
00:26:48,270 --> 00:26:49,310
That's why I need to interview you

638
00:26:49,310 --> 00:26:50,370
and your daughter.

639
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:55,330
How many years have you been a journalist?

640
00:26:55,680 --> 00:26:56,270
8 months.

641
00:26:59,310 --> 00:27:00,170
Let me tell you.

642
00:27:00,750 --> 00:27:01,400
A journalist's duty

643
00:27:01,400 --> 00:27:02,590
is to pursue the truth

644
00:27:02,590 --> 00:27:04,120
and reconstruct the truth.

645
00:27:05,200 --> 00:27:06,640
So if you don't have evidence,

646
00:27:06,640 --> 00:27:07,900
don't write nonsense.

647
00:27:09,880 --> 00:27:11,940
-Then you…
-Why are you following me?

648
00:27:12,350 --> 00:27:13,610
You know my dad, right?

649
00:27:17,680 --> 00:27:18,540
Who is your dad?

650
00:27:19,070 --> 00:27:19,640
Zhou Pu,

651
00:27:20,310 --> 00:27:22,110
the lawyer for Yan Jicai's case.

652
00:27:24,160 --> 00:27:25,160
I don't remember.

653
00:27:27,030 --> 00:27:27,550
Then at least you can

654
00:27:27,550 --> 00:27:28,980
talk about that case, right?

655
00:27:28,980 --> 00:27:29,920
You're already retired.

656
00:27:29,920 --> 00:27:31,520
That case was explosive too.

657
00:27:31,640 --> 00:27:32,680
Carrying two wrongful convictions,

658
00:27:32,680 --> 00:27:33,640
don't you feel the weight?

659
00:27:33,640 --> 00:27:34,760
Since your daughter was wronged,

660
00:27:34,760 --> 00:27:35,440
could Yan Jicai also

661
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:36,000
have been wronged?

662
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:37,270
Have you ever thought...

663
00:27:37,270 --> 00:27:38,160
Are you done?

664
00:27:50,550 --> 00:27:52,070
Hu Xudong, to be honest,

665
00:27:52,090 --> 00:27:53,570
is a bit of a hothead.

666
00:27:55,720 --> 00:27:56,880
Why do you say that too?

667
00:27:56,880 --> 00:27:58,140
I'm just reminding you

668
00:27:58,400 --> 00:27:59,270
that sometimes, when you look

669
00:27:59,270 --> 00:28:00,000
at things from a different angle,

670
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:01,660
you can understand a lot more.

671
00:28:03,720 --> 00:28:04,550
You...

672
00:28:05,640 --> 00:28:07,570
really are different from before.

673
00:28:08,640 --> 00:28:09,840
Is that a compliment?

674
00:28:10,160 --> 00:28:10,760
Of course.

675
00:28:14,310 --> 00:28:15,770
So what are you going to do?

676
00:28:19,070 --> 00:28:20,670
I have to convince him first.

677
00:28:21,160 --> 00:28:21,960
If I want him

678
00:28:21,960 --> 00:28:22,910
to believe me,

679
00:28:23,440 --> 00:28:25,040
I need to show him something.

680
00:28:26,790 --> 00:28:28,590
Where are you planning to start?

681
00:28:29,200 --> 00:28:30,400
I'll go to the village first

682
00:28:30,400 --> 00:28:32,130
and start from the crime scene.

683
00:28:33,620 --> 00:28:36,950
You just have to make this little bit
of money from my family,

684
00:28:37,070 --> 00:28:37,670
don't you?

685
00:28:38,440 --> 00:28:39,510
I don't want money.

686
00:28:39,880 --> 00:28:40,680
It's free.

687
00:28:43,070 --> 00:28:45,330
Your fiancée called off the engagement.

688
00:28:46,070 --> 00:28:47,330
As for the bride price,

689
00:28:48,590 --> 00:28:50,720
I managed to get half of it back for you.

690
00:28:56,680 --> 00:28:58,010
Can I smoke a cigarette?

691
00:28:58,200 --> 00:28:59,000
I don't smoke.

692
00:29:06,240 --> 00:29:06,750
Fine.

693
00:29:08,590 --> 00:29:09,110
Fine.

694
00:29:10,550 --> 00:29:12,160
Please tell my father

695
00:29:13,350 --> 00:29:14,350
that the money...

696
00:29:16,960 --> 00:29:19,020
can be used for my brother's wedding.

697
00:29:19,240 --> 00:29:20,100
I won't need it.

698
00:29:20,440 --> 00:29:21,030
Are you just going

699
00:29:21,030 --> 00:29:22,830
to give up on yourself like this?

700
00:29:26,270 --> 00:29:27,930
Yin Ping's grandmother died.

701
00:29:29,720 --> 00:29:31,650
Not long after you were brought in,

702
00:29:33,070 --> 00:29:36,000
the old lady hanged herself
at the village entrance.

703
00:29:38,310 --> 00:29:39,710
So I want to tell you this.

704
00:29:41,550 --> 00:29:42,400
If

705
00:29:43,000 --> 00:29:45,130
you just give up on yourself like this,

706
00:29:45,210 --> 00:29:46,560
the deaths of Yin Ping

707
00:29:46,590 --> 00:29:47,310
and his grandmother

708
00:29:47,310 --> 00:29:49,110
may both rest on your shoulders.

709
00:29:49,240 --> 00:29:51,960
Even if you can hide in prison
for the rest of your life

710
00:29:51,960 --> 00:29:53,030
and don't care,

711
00:29:53,720 --> 00:29:55,050
what about your father?

712
00:29:55,350 --> 00:29:56,750
What about your brother?

713
00:29:57,160 --> 00:29:59,420
With you carrying the name of a murderer,

714
00:29:59,720 --> 00:30:01,920
do you think your brother can find a wife

715
00:30:02,480 --> 00:30:04,110
with that little bit of bride price?

716
00:30:04,110 --> 00:30:05,790
Are you going
to let them live their whole lives

717
00:30:05,790 --> 00:30:07,590
with their heads down in that village?

718
00:30:07,590 --> 00:30:08,160
I...

719
00:30:09,750 --> 00:30:10,610
I don't know...

720
00:30:12,790 --> 00:30:14,160
what else I can do.

721
00:30:14,350 --> 00:30:15,510
I'm here to help you.

722
00:30:15,970 --> 00:30:17,430
I just came from the scene.

723
00:30:17,750 --> 00:30:19,720
They're going to build a road there,

724
00:30:19,720 --> 00:30:21,510
so the longer your case drags on,

725
00:30:21,510 --> 00:30:22,770
the worse it is for you.

726
00:30:22,880 --> 00:30:24,030
What I need to do now

727
00:30:24,760 --> 00:30:26,480
is reconstruct what actually happened

728
00:30:26,480 --> 00:30:28,110
that night as soon as possible.

729
00:30:28,110 --> 00:30:29,070
Helping me now

730
00:30:29,960 --> 00:30:31,160
is helping yourself.

731
00:30:31,980 --> 00:30:33,840
The sooner I can get into this case

732
00:30:34,350 --> 00:30:35,510
and see the files,

733
00:30:36,270 --> 00:30:37,600
the better it is for you.

734
00:30:37,960 --> 00:30:38,960
You know the law.

735
00:30:39,440 --> 00:30:41,440
You understand all this, don't you?

736
00:30:43,440 --> 00:30:44,750
I'm a bit confused.

737
00:30:46,440 --> 00:30:48,040
We're not related in any way.

738
00:30:48,310 --> 00:30:49,370
What are you after?

739
00:30:50,200 --> 00:30:52,000
Why are you helping me like this?

740
00:30:55,680 --> 00:30:56,410
For a chance.

741
00:30:57,790 --> 00:30:59,190
Giving yourself a chance

742
00:31:00,680 --> 00:31:01,880
is giving me a chance.

743
00:31:11,440 --> 00:31:12,510
Let me defend you.

744
00:31:15,390 --> 00:31:16,520
[Defense Authorization Letter]

745
00:32:01,270 --> 00:32:02,000
Yizhong.

746
00:32:34,550 --> 00:32:35,080
Yizhong.

747
00:32:36,510 --> 00:32:38,310
Get up. Wash up before you sleep.

748
00:32:41,830 --> 00:32:43,230
Why haven't you left yet?

749
00:32:43,240 --> 00:32:44,640
Where am I supposed to go?

750
00:32:46,120 --> 00:32:47,800
You need to move back to the dorm.

751
00:32:47,800 --> 00:32:49,170
Now I'm officially

752
00:32:49,200 --> 00:32:50,590
Hu Xudong's defense lawyer,

753
00:32:50,590 --> 00:32:51,160
so it's definitely improper

754
00:32:51,160 --> 00:32:52,490
for us to live together.

755
00:32:52,790 --> 00:32:55,390
I told you I wouldn't get involved
in that case.

756
00:32:56,030 --> 00:32:57,290
It's not about whether you're involved.

757
00:32:57,290 --> 00:32:58,880
Normally, given our relationship,

758
00:32:58,880 --> 00:33:00,640
even discussing the case privately
is improper.

759
00:33:00,640 --> 00:33:01,440
You know that?

760
00:33:02,440 --> 00:33:03,500
Our relationship?

761
00:33:04,350 --> 00:33:05,880
What relationship is that?

762
00:33:13,270 --> 00:33:15,730
Anyway, living together is inappropriate.

763
00:33:17,720 --> 00:33:18,440
I've said

764
00:33:19,640 --> 00:33:21,110
I'll leave after tonight.

765
00:34:18,520 --> 00:34:19,480
What benefits did the two of them

766
00:34:19,480 --> 00:34:20,699
give you?

767
00:34:21,960 --> 00:34:23,889
It's the instinct of a journalist.

768
00:34:24,030 --> 00:34:25,139
I also want to know the truth.

769
00:34:25,139 --> 00:34:26,199
Is there a problem?

770
00:34:30,070 --> 00:34:30,710
Mr. Zhou.

771
00:34:31,280 --> 00:34:32,600
Please don't feel pressured.

772
00:34:32,600 --> 00:34:33,560
We came to see you

773
00:34:33,590 --> 00:34:34,920
because we wanted to ask

774
00:34:35,190 --> 00:34:37,150
if there were any details
you might have forgotten

775
00:34:37,150 --> 00:34:38,350
to mention back then.

776
00:34:39,639 --> 00:34:40,480
Everything I had to say

777
00:34:40,480 --> 00:34:42,960
is in the defense statement.

778
00:34:43,400 --> 00:34:44,480
You got drunk once

779
00:34:44,480 --> 00:34:46,409
and mentioned someone named Qiao…

780
00:35:01,360 --> 00:35:02,360
I'm getting old.

781
00:35:02,930 --> 00:35:03,810
My mind

782
00:35:03,840 --> 00:35:04,860
can't hold onto so many

783
00:35:04,860 --> 00:35:06,050
useless things.

784
00:35:09,060 --> 00:35:10,520
Pick up the slipper for me!

785
00:35:21,590 --> 00:35:22,990
What is the relationship

786
00:35:23,150 --> 00:35:24,280
between you two now?

787
00:35:26,190 --> 00:35:27,110
She's been transferred

788
00:35:27,110 --> 00:35:28,370
to our procuratorate.

789
00:35:28,590 --> 00:35:29,650
She's my superior.

790
00:35:31,320 --> 00:35:32,850
I've got plenty of time now.

791
00:35:33,960 --> 00:35:35,960
I can keep coming back to bother you.

792
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:40,530
Mr. Zhou.

793
00:35:41,550 --> 00:35:43,550
This is a recent photo of Yan Jicai.

794
00:35:48,070 --> 00:35:49,200
He is only in his 40s.

795
00:35:52,420 --> 00:35:54,270
He looks really old.

796
00:35:55,440 --> 00:35:56,370
What do you mean?

797
00:35:56,800 --> 00:35:58,070
Is this my fault?

798
00:35:59,840 --> 00:36:00,760
In prison,

799
00:36:01,110 --> 00:36:02,550
he's been refusing to confess

800
00:36:02,550 --> 00:36:04,360
and doesn't accept a reduced sentence,

801
00:36:04,360 --> 00:36:06,360
because he says he's not a criminal.

802
00:36:07,800 --> 00:36:08,710
He's got at least

803
00:36:08,710 --> 00:36:10,510
15 more years in Bieshan Prison.

804
00:36:10,550 --> 00:36:12,010
His daughter is seven now.

805
00:36:12,190 --> 00:36:14,790
By then, she will have graduated
from college.

806
00:36:15,320 --> 00:36:16,280
And my mentor

807
00:36:17,110 --> 00:36:18,000
is almost 60.

808
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:19,920
He has been stationed

809
00:36:19,920 --> 00:36:21,650
at Bieshan Prison for 28 years.

810
00:36:21,960 --> 00:36:23,360
Because of this case,

811
00:36:24,150 --> 00:36:26,550
he voluntarily postponed his retirement,

812
00:36:27,760 --> 00:36:29,400
living apart from his wife.

813
00:36:29,590 --> 00:36:30,190
No one knows

814
00:36:30,190 --> 00:36:32,190
how much longer he must endure this.

815
00:36:33,150 --> 00:36:34,030
Mr. Zhou.

816
00:36:35,290 --> 00:36:37,950
I won't lecture you
on high‑minded principles.

817
00:36:38,970 --> 00:36:40,400
If you don't want to give a single hair
to benefit the world,

818
00:36:40,400 --> 00:36:41,480
that's fine.

819
00:36:42,480 --> 00:36:44,090
But could you at least say one more word

820
00:36:44,090 --> 00:36:45,190
for a father with a 7-year-old daughter

821
00:36:45,190 --> 00:36:46,320
who might have been

822
00:36:46,320 --> 00:36:48,230
wrongfully convicted and is going

823
00:36:48,230 --> 00:36:49,490
to serve over 20 years?

824
00:36:50,040 --> 00:36:50,880
Are you not even willing

825
00:36:50,880 --> 00:36:52,010
to say one more word?

826
00:36:52,710 --> 00:36:54,070
You have a daughter too.

827
00:36:58,320 --> 00:36:58,880
Dad.

828
00:36:59,230 --> 00:36:59,880
Shut up!

829
00:37:01,840 --> 00:37:02,360
Get out!

830
00:37:14,430 --> 00:37:16,560
Would you die if you said one more word?

831
00:37:21,590 --> 00:37:22,720
I'll leave it to you.

832
00:37:22,880 --> 00:37:23,480
Thank you.

833
00:37:28,320 --> 00:37:28,960
No rush.

834
00:37:29,710 --> 00:37:31,570
I told you I've got plenty of time.

835
00:37:33,110 --> 00:37:35,440
You are prosecutors.

836
00:37:36,880 --> 00:37:37,880
I am a lawyer.

837
00:37:39,640 --> 00:37:42,200
Especially in front of you,

838
00:37:42,230 --> 00:37:44,510
I can't irresponsibly spout

839
00:37:44,530 --> 00:37:46,260
my own speculations.

840
00:37:48,400 --> 00:37:50,600
Speculation may not count as evidence,

841
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:53,110
yet it can become a lead.

842
00:37:59,960 --> 00:38:02,360
I've been handling cases
for so many years.

843
00:38:02,510 --> 00:38:04,170
I've seen all kinds of people.

844
00:38:04,320 --> 00:38:05,190
Over the years,

845
00:38:06,030 --> 00:38:07,890
I've picked up a bit of intuition.

846
00:38:11,710 --> 00:38:13,310
Just pretend I'm hypnotized

847
00:38:13,960 --> 00:38:15,290
and talking in my sleep.

848
00:38:21,140 --> 00:38:23,700
Lin Yan had a boyfriend

849
00:38:23,720 --> 00:38:24,930
named Qiao Xiaojun.

850
00:38:24,960 --> 00:38:26,920
You both remember him, right?

851
00:38:28,230 --> 00:38:29,690
You remember everything.

852
00:38:30,230 --> 00:38:32,030
Of course. I have a great memory.

853
00:38:32,450 --> 00:38:33,650
Stop messing with me.

854
00:38:35,150 --> 00:38:36,670
I think Qiao Xiaojun

855
00:38:37,530 --> 00:38:39,730
must have seen

856
00:38:39,760 --> 00:38:41,550
or heard something.

857
00:38:43,840 --> 00:38:44,630
What?

858
00:38:45,630 --> 00:38:47,150
According to his statement,

859
00:38:47,150 --> 00:38:48,760
he got heavily drunk that night,

860
00:38:48,760 --> 00:38:50,440
went to bed early,
and turned off his pager.

861
00:38:50,440 --> 00:38:52,190
He claimed he didn't hear

862
00:38:52,210 --> 00:38:53,610
and see anything, right?

863
00:38:53,610 --> 00:38:54,440
Right.

864
00:38:55,230 --> 00:38:56,510
Most likely,

865
00:38:59,440 --> 00:39:01,920
he was lying.

866
00:39:16,230 --> 00:39:16,800
Stop!

867
00:39:18,760 --> 00:39:19,320
Stop!

868
00:39:20,030 --> 00:39:20,670
Stop!

869
00:39:21,360 --> 00:39:23,090
What did you promise Zhou Tong?

870
00:39:24,110 --> 00:39:24,630
Hurry!

871
00:39:24,800 --> 00:39:25,930
-Drive!
-Slow down!

872
00:39:26,400 --> 00:39:27,070
Drive!

873
00:39:27,320 --> 00:39:29,070
What benefits did they give you this time?

874
00:39:29,070 --> 00:39:30,070
Stop right there!

875
00:39:55,480 --> 00:39:56,400
Both you and your father

876
00:39:56,400 --> 00:39:57,400
are pretty agile.

877
00:39:58,380 --> 00:39:59,440
Do you know
what the most important quality is

878
00:39:59,440 --> 00:40:01,370
for an investigative journalist?

879
00:40:01,800 --> 00:40:03,510
Pursuing the truth and never giving up?

880
00:40:03,510 --> 00:40:04,760
It's running fast.

881
00:40:05,280 --> 00:40:07,540
Otherwise, you'll always get beaten up.

882
00:40:10,640 --> 00:40:11,060
Right.

883
00:40:11,550 --> 00:40:12,680
About that article,

884
00:40:12,880 --> 00:40:14,280
when can we talk about it?

885
00:40:16,160 --> 00:40:17,000
What article?

886
00:40:18,550 --> 00:40:19,610
He didn't tell you?

887
00:40:22,280 --> 00:40:23,710
I didn't promise you anything.

888
00:40:23,710 --> 00:40:25,370
I just said I'd think about it.

889
00:40:25,760 --> 00:40:26,400
Did we pinky swear?

890
00:40:26,400 --> 00:40:27,200
No, we didn't.

891
00:40:27,840 --> 00:40:29,030
Zheng Jianmin, you...

892
00:40:29,030 --> 00:40:31,360
A journalist also needs another quality.

893
00:40:31,400 --> 00:40:32,660
Don't be too trusting.

894
00:40:36,030 --> 00:40:36,890
Lihui,

895
00:40:37,320 --> 00:40:38,780
keep your husband in line.

896
00:40:40,280 --> 00:40:41,440
Are you really going to write it?

897
00:40:41,440 --> 00:40:42,550
I really am.

898
00:40:43,070 --> 00:40:44,440
It might even help you.

899
00:40:45,010 --> 00:40:45,710
Don't underestimate

900
00:40:45,710 --> 00:40:47,570
the power of serious journalism.

901
00:40:51,230 --> 00:40:52,290
Prosecutor Zhang,

902
00:40:53,040 --> 00:40:53,840
this is not a joke.

903
00:40:53,840 --> 00:40:55,240
Please think carefully.

904
00:40:56,690 --> 00:40:57,890
Let me think about it.

905
00:41:11,070 --> 00:41:11,710
Everyone.

906
00:41:12,760 --> 00:41:13,670
Because of my

907
00:41:13,760 --> 00:41:15,400
success in handling this case,

908
00:41:15,400 --> 00:41:16,880
our firm's practice

909
00:41:17,550 --> 00:41:19,810
has expanded into non-litigation work.

910
00:41:19,840 --> 00:41:21,150
I am very happy.

911
00:41:26,320 --> 00:41:26,920
Of course,

912
00:41:27,030 --> 00:41:28,320
this couldn't have happened

913
00:41:28,320 --> 00:41:29,440
without Mr. Li's support

914
00:41:29,440 --> 00:41:30,300
and everyone's

915
00:41:30,630 --> 00:41:31,510
recognition.

916
00:41:32,230 --> 00:41:33,000
Tonight,

917
00:41:33,800 --> 00:41:34,800
I'm treating everyone to dinner

918
00:41:34,800 --> 00:41:35,930
out of my own pocket.

919
00:41:36,400 --> 00:41:37,480
Luming Restaurant,

920
00:41:37,480 --> 00:41:39,390
a Sichuan eatery
owned by a friend of mine.

921
00:41:39,390 --> 00:41:40,550
There are private rooms.

922
00:41:40,550 --> 00:41:41,440
At 7 PM.

923
00:41:41,960 --> 00:41:42,920
Everyone, please come.

924
00:41:42,920 --> 00:41:44,250
Everyone, please come.

925
00:41:45,360 --> 00:41:45,960
Zhao,

926
00:41:47,070 --> 00:41:47,800
you come too.

927
00:41:53,880 --> 00:41:55,140
What's wrong with him?

928
00:41:55,190 --> 00:41:56,650
Acting like he's the boss.

929
00:41:59,480 --> 00:42:01,210
If someone's paying, just eat.

930
00:42:01,630 --> 00:42:02,960
No, there's nothing to talk about.

931
00:42:02,960 --> 00:42:03,860
Look, at the entrance of your workplace,

932
00:42:03,860 --> 00:42:05,440
it doesn't look good
grabbing at each other.

933
00:42:05,440 --> 00:42:06,030
Let's just

934
00:42:06,030 --> 00:42:07,280
have a quick chat inside the car.

935
00:42:07,280 --> 00:42:08,000
Be careful.

936
00:42:08,280 --> 00:42:08,480
Wait.

937
00:42:08,480 --> 00:42:09,550
Why are you
driving the official car?

938
00:42:09,550 --> 00:42:11,190
It's fine. There are no outsiders.

939
00:42:11,190 --> 00:42:11,670
Come on.

940
00:42:12,360 --> 00:42:12,890
Sit here.

941
00:42:21,030 --> 00:42:23,630
I really don't want
to talk about this anymore.

942
00:42:23,960 --> 00:42:25,490
Can you just leave me alone?

943
00:42:27,190 --> 00:42:28,720
I'm the one looking for you.

944
00:42:30,630 --> 00:42:31,490
And who are you?

945
00:42:31,960 --> 00:42:32,760
A journalist.

946
00:42:34,280 --> 00:42:35,440
I've been tracking and investigating
this case

947
00:42:35,440 --> 00:42:36,300
for a long time.

948
00:42:36,400 --> 00:42:37,530
You are a key figure.

949
00:42:38,670 --> 00:42:39,280
Me?

950
00:42:39,800 --> 00:42:40,630
A key figure?

951
00:42:41,440 --> 00:42:42,110
Wait, how am I

952
00:42:42,110 --> 00:42:42,920
a key figure?

953
00:42:43,720 --> 00:42:45,230
Lin Yan died because she was going

954
00:42:45,230 --> 00:42:46,000
to see you.

955
00:42:46,040 --> 00:42:46,710
And

956
00:42:47,230 --> 00:42:48,110
after that,

957
00:42:48,280 --> 00:42:50,340
instead of feeling guilt or remorse,

958
00:42:50,480 --> 00:42:52,510
you hid the truth to protect yourself.

959
00:42:52,510 --> 00:42:53,960
That's equivalent to you and the killer

960
00:42:53,960 --> 00:42:54,480
murdering Lin Yan together.

961
00:42:54,480 --> 00:42:55,000
Wait, wait! Shut up!

962
00:42:55,000 --> 00:42:55,400
Shut up!

963
00:42:55,400 --> 00:42:56,510
Stop talking nonsense!

964
00:42:56,510 --> 00:42:57,820
What kind of journalist are you?

965
00:42:57,820 --> 00:42:58,760
Believe me, I'll sue you!

966
00:42:58,760 --> 00:42:59,820
Go ahead and sue me.

967
00:42:59,880 --> 00:43:00,590
That'll make me famous.

968
00:43:00,590 --> 00:43:01,150
If I were afraid of that,

969
00:43:01,150 --> 00:43:02,110
I would have quit this job long ago.
